I am on the bed.
I take my phone.
I connect to the room's wifi.
I make an audio call to Mexico.
My parents are on the phone.
My mother asks, "Maya, how are you?"
I say, "Mom, I am fine."
I ask, "How are you?"
My father says, "We are fine."
He asks, "Maya, where are you now?"
I say, "I am in my room now."
"Is the room good?" my mother asks.
I answer, "Yes, the room is very nice."
Dad asks, "Are you safe?"
I say, "Yes Dad, I am perfectly safe."
They are a little worried.
But now they are happy.
Everything is fine here in Mumbai.
I hang up the phone.
